## v1.0.0b4

Changes since v1.0.0b3:

+ Add an IHEP HepJob runner backend.
  - Run the workflow coordinator and every Snakemake rule through `hep_sub`, track and
    cancel coordinator/child jobs, and retain their jobscripts and logs.
  - Translate Celebi memory limits to HepJob resources and keep runtime state on the
    shared workflow filesystem so jobs can move between worker nodes.
  - Add runner probing, transfer/cache/purge integration, installation documentation,
    and `scripts/setup-ihep-runner.sh`.
  - Provide a real `script` Conda environment and fail explicitly when it is unavailable.
+ Make workflow submission lifecycle-aware and idempotent.
  - Reuse active workflows (including `unknown` SSH launches) and completed results.
  - Replace failed, dissonant, or stopped workflows while retaining immutable predecessor
    workflow/status metadata in the submission record.
  - Initialize job metadata for the requested runner before reading workflow state.
  - Support guarded unknown-workflow resubmission: refresh first and replace only after
    failure is confirmed.
+ Add synchronous live status refresh for Celebi's `status --wait`.
  - `GET /status/<project>/<impression>?wait=true` waits for the shared refresh lock,
    queries the runner, propagates the new state, and then returns it.
  - Coordinate live HTTP refreshes with queued Celery refreshes without leaving stale
    queue markers; return refresh failures explicitly to the client.
+ Keep delayed SSH launches pollable.
  - Use `unknown` when neither the startup nor exit marker is visible yet, then promote
    the workflow when later evidence confirms that it started.
+ Harden workflow cache publication and dependency diagnostics.
  - Fence failed/stopped SSH and IHEP workspaces so stale workflows cannot republish a
    purged cache; publish completed caches atomically with completion markers.
  - Persist structured `blocked_by` snapshots limited to each job's submitted ancestry.
+ Allow explicit collection of failed-workflow stageout as clearly marked diagnostic,
  unofficial output while retaining logs-only collection as the default.
+ Reorganize Yuki by responsibility.
  - Split kernel code into `jobs`, `workflows`, `runners`, `execution`, and `storage`;
    move application operations to `Yuki.services`, server-only code to
    `Yuki.server.services`, and shared helpers to `Yuki.utils`.
  - Remove the obsolete flat kernel modules after migrating production code and tests.
+ Improve the Conda-based RabbitMQ setup.
  - Add the setup script, reduce environment-solver memory use, locate the conda-forge
    binary reliably, and enable Celery-compatible RabbitMQ behavior.
+ Set the Yuki package version to `1.0.0b4`.
